# 18. The radio's title: its sprites and colours (section 14.6). >> at 3300: the title object ($1958E)
#     runs from 3301; each tick it calls $11C66 with R18 = the text, R3 = y << 16 | x, R5 = the palette
#     word $197CD[(D >> 1) & 7] (D counted first): $80 at 3301, $C0 at 3303 and 3305, $A0, $A0, $B0, ..
#     $11C66 writes one sprite a character (the header at $122B5C; the character's address $A861 + 8c).
#     The palettes $80-$FF (palette RAM as xBBBBBGGGGGRRRRR) are those of the data ROM's record at
#     $153904. The screenshots: 3320 the title at x = 66 + 80 in palette $D0 (the tick of 3317),
#     3331 at 21 + 80 in $F0, 3332 and 3333 at 15 + 80 in $F0, 3334 at 10 + 80 in $80, 3400 held at 80
#     in $80 (the font, the colours and the position are checked on every frame by
#     tools/orradiotest -screen).
include race_mp.inc
3300-3305 set P2_A 04 1
3306 set P2_A 04 0
3300 bp $11C66 24
3300 mem $122B5C 16
3300 mem $197CD 16
3320 snap e18_3320.png
3331 snap e18_3331.png
3332 snap e18_3332.png
3333 snap e18_3333.png
3334 snap e18_3334.png
3340 pal 0 $80 $80
3400 snap e18_3400.png
3410 exit
